  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two circles with equal radii are intersecting at the points (0,1) and (0,-1) . The tangent at the point (0,1) to one of the circles passes through the centre of the other circle. Then the distance between the centres of these circles is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NjVnE",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hW2IB",
      "text": "2",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "imMW5",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4gGSd",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because$ Two circles of equal radii intersect each other orthogonally. Then $R$ is mid point of $P Q$.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/It98ThH9yhsWCG9y11iji5ubWkYTbSxAuT0axtFY03s.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nand $P R=O_{1} R=O_{2} R$\r\n\r\n$P R=\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{(0-0)^{2}+(1+1)^{2}}=1$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ Distance between centres $=1+1=2$.",
    "image": null
  },
